    "text": "How many of the statement(s) are correct<br />\ri) The nucleophile makes a rear attack in <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mtext>N</mtext> </msub> <mtext>2</mtext></mrow> </math> reaction and expels the leaving group from front side.<br />\rii) <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> adds to <math> <mrow> <mtext>HBr</mtext></mrow> </math> according to Anti‐Markownikoff’s rule.<br />\riii) The basicity of halides decreases in the order <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> but the nucleophillicity is reverse of it. (in polar protic solvents)<br />\riv) The rate of <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mtext>N</mtext> </msub> <mtext>2</mtext></mrow> </math> reaction is independent of the polarity of the solvent.<br />\rv) Sigma complex or arenium ion is resonance stablised.",
